  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.repositories.mongodb.models.Dealer\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A MongoDB document model class representing a dealer entity in the 'dealers' collection. This class serves as a persistence layer model that bridges between MongoDB and the domain layer. Key fields include: an @Id annotated 'id' field (MongoDB document identifier), an @Indexed 'name' field (optimized for queries), and additional dealer information fields (contact, address, email, phone). The class provides two constructors: a default no-arg constructor and a constructor that accepts a DealerInfo domain object to populate the fields. The primary conversion method toDealerInfo() transforms this MongoDB document back into a DealerInfo domain object, enabling clean separation between persistence and domain models. Standard getId() and setId() methods manage the MongoDB document identifier.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/repositories/mongodb/models/Dealer.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
